---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import BuildUpLink from "../../components/UnderTheHood/BuildUpLink.astro"
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro"
import Example from "../../components/Example/index"
import StartingStyleCompare from "../../components/Learn/StartingStyleCompare.astro"
import Basics from "../../component-examples/drawer/Basics.astro"
---

<TechniquePost slug="drawer-starting-style">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A slide-in panel used to be a fixed <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> with a transform,
      plus JavaScript for the focus trap, <kbd>Esc</kbd>, backdrop clicks and an
      inert page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Animating it out was the hard part: <code>display: none</code> can't transition,
      so a class had to be removed only after
      {" "}<code>transitionend</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The drawer is a modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, pinned to an edge
        with <code>margin: 0</code> and logical insets
      </li>
      <li>
        Closed, it waits just past its edge with <code>translate</code>. Open,
        it sits at <code>translate: 0 0</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>@starting-style</code> repeats the closed position, so opening slides
        in from there
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>allow-discrete</code> on <code>display</code> and
        {" "}<code>overlay</code> keeps it rendered and in the top layer until it
        has slid out
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>--dir</code> flips to <code>-1</code> under
        {" "}<code>:dir(rtl)</code>, so the start edge works both ways
      </li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`.drawer {
  inset-inline-end: auto;
  inset-inline-start: 0;
  transition:
    display 0.3s allow-discrete,
    overlay 0.3s allow-discrete,
    translate 0.3s;
  translate: calc(-100% * var(--dir)) 0;
}

.drawer[open] {
  translate: 0 0;

  @starting-style {
    translate: calc(-100% * var(--dir)) 0;
  }
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <p>
      Two panels with the drawer's transition. Only one has <code
        >@starting-style</code
      >. Open and close them together.
    </p>
    <Example wide showCode={false}>
      <StartingStyleCompare />
    </Example>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Both leave the same way: <code>allow-discrete</code> keeps the panel displayed
        until the slide ends
      </li>
      <li>
        Only the one with <code>@starting-style</code> slides in. The other goes from
        <code>display: none</code> to its open position with nothing to transition
        from, so it appears in place
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Open a drawer from each edge and watch it slide out again.</p>
    <Example column showCode={false}>
      <Basics />
    </Example>
    <BuildUpLink />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Without <code>@starting-style</code> and <code>allow-discrete</code> the drawer
        opens and closes instantly, and still works as a modal
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>overlay</code> is Chromium only. Elsewhere the drawer leaves the top
        layer as soon as it closes, so the backdrop goes at once while the drawer
        slides out
      </li>
      <li>
        Without <code>closedby</code> it still closes on <kbd>Esc</kbd>, but not
        on a click outside
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
